.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_SESSION_HAS_TICKET 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_SESSION_get0_ticket ,
.Nm SSL_SESSION_has_ticket ,
.Nm SSL_SESSION_get_ticket_lifetime_hint
.Nd get details about the ticket associated with a session
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_SESSION_has_ticket
.Fa "const SSL_SESSION *s"
.Fc
.Ft unsigned long
.Fo SSL_SESSION_get_ticket_lifetime_hint
.Fa "const SSL_SESSION *s"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_SESSION_get0_ticket
.Fa "const SSL_SESSION *s"
.Fa "const unsigned char **tick"
.Fa "size_t *len"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_SESSION_has_ticket
returns 1 if there is a Session Ticket associated with this session, and
0 otherwise.
.Pp
SSL_SESSION_get_ticket_lifetime_hint returns the lifetime hint in
seconds associated with the session ticket.
.Pp
SSL_SESSION_get0_ticket obtains a pointer to the ticket associated with
a session.
The length of the ticket is written to
.Sy *len .
If
.Fa tick
is non NULL then a pointer to the ticket is written to
.Sy *tick .
The pointer is only valid while the connection is in use.
The session (and hence the ticket pointer) may also become invalid as a
result of a call to
.Xr SSL_CTX_flush_sessions 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SSL_SESSION_has_ticket
returns 1 if session ticket exists or 0 otherwise.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_SESSION_get_ticket_lifetime_hint
returns the number of seconds.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssl 7 ,
.Xr d2i_SSL_SESSION 3 ,
.Xr SSL_SESSION_get_time 3 ,
.Xr SSL_SESSION_free 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn SSL_SESSION_has_ticket ,
.Fn SSL_SESSION_get_ticket_lifetime_hint
and
.Fn SSL_SESSION_get0_ticket
functions were added in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
